Amy wrote:

> Okay, you really need to get another Cloak of Magic Resistance.
> Magicbane and the Eye are not enough - some monsters in Gehennom like
> to steal nice artifacts that you have, leaving you without magic
> protection.  A +5 CoMR is vital, in my opinion.

Opinions on this differ: two (stealable) sources is almost always good
enough.

> You also should really practice your divination spells a little more
> - magic mapping is indispensible in Gehennom, as is detect treasure.

Again, opinions differ widely on this. Personally, I *never* use magic
mapping, especially not in Gehennom, since I happen to like mapping it
out by "sticking to the left/right wall". This ensures that you visit
every spot on the level, and not making shortcuts right from the
beginning will also prevent monsters being able to get down on you from
more than one direction.

>> 2. Should I use a wish on a robe? I lost my CoMR to a polymorph
>> accident (but it was fun being a dragon for a while!), but I assume
>> with EotA and MB I can do without it. On the other hand, the elven
>> cloak gives me stealth, which is nice.

> See above. I would wish on a new CoMR.  Its indispensible.

See above. You might go for a cloak of displacement instead (but note
that this only grants a magic cancellation of 2, not 3).

>> 3. How can I get my spell fail rates down, in particular FoD?  My
>> attack spell level is currently skilled, will going to expert do it?

Finger of death is highly overrated. It drains your mana, especially
after you've got hold of the Amulet of Yendor. Magic missile is the
special spell for wizards, and is much more economical. It may not do
the same amount of instant damage, but you can cast it 3.5 times as
often for the same cost.

For instant kills, carry wands of death. If you are a neutral wizard,
and don't mind wishing for other classes' Quest artifacts, wish for the
Platinum Yendorian Express Card, and those wands will be even more
effective.

> It should do.  Practice makes perfect, after all. I don't think you
> can get to expert in all spells though.

Indeed. Note that there are two reasons: (1) you don't have enough skill
slots for this, even when you reach level 30, and (2) a wizard cannot
reach expert in every spell group (only in attack, divination, escape
and matter, while he can get to skilled in healing, enchantment and
divination).

>> 4. Does EotA work in Gehennom?  How about after I have the Amulet of
>> Yendor?

> Yes, it does.  However,  the AoY does strange things to mana
> regeneration. After you have the AoY you wont be able to use too many
> spells.

After you get the Amulet of Yendor, you can no longer level teleport, no
matter if you use the Eye of the Aethiopica for this or try another
means.

> I would say you should get a CoMR before the castle.

That's three times... Again, this is a matter of taste, and *even* if
both the Eye and Magicbane would be stolen at the same time (not even
*one* of those has ever happened to me), that doesn't mean you'll be
killed immediately, before you can get them back...

Don't get me wrong, I think the cloak is desireable, but I also think it
is by no means as necessary as you imply.

> Most importantly, you shouldn't be burdened.

I couldn't agree more.

> Try to identify all your stuff - maybe
> you can wish up a spellbook of identify, or polymorph one of your
> others and hope for the best.

Again, very true. The spellbook of identify is one of the most potent
items in the game, not only for wizards, but for all classes that can
cast it more or less reliably.

> Used up wands, useless wands (secret door detection, nothing, speed
> monster), duplicates of rings or amulets. Also, a spellbook of light
> would be nice - Gehennom is a dark place. Otherwise, you seem to be
> well prepared.

A spellbook of light is not too useful, I think: for my characters, its
main use is to practice divination spells so I can better cast identify
lateron.

For Gehennom, a magic lamp is much more useful. Unfortunately, the
original poster mentioned he has already misused two of those by using
them for a wish... He really should have kept one of those as a
permanent light source.

